.TH SDL_GetJoystickName 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetJoystickName \- Get the implementation dependent name of a joystick.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetJoystickName(SDL_Joystick *joystick);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I joystick
the
.BR SDL_Joystick
obtained from
.BR SDL_OpenJoystick ()\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the name of the selected joystick\[char46] If no name can be found, this function returns NULL; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetJoystickNameForID (3)
